        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T17:46:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that the state machine probably already has all of the information needed to do this at the right time. What if we moved the `tc_detached` calls to the non-PRS cases in `attached_snk_exit` and `attached_src_exit`, `ct_attached_snk_exit`, and `restart_tc_sm`?",
      "revId": "d17e7f95f390ef91a87088544044bb389d668b39",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23863890_e412c60a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 2177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T21:01:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Moving `tc_detached()` to the `attached_*_exit` functions and `restart_tc_sm()` runs into two issues:\n\n1. `ctx-\u003ecurrent` has not updated yet in exit functions: `set_state()` calls exit functions before updating `ctx-\u003ecurrent \u003d new_state`. When `tc_detached()` fires `HOOK_USB_PD_DISCONNECT` from `tc_attached_*_exit()`, `pd_is_disconnected(port)` is still false.\n2. Not all non-PRS exits from Attached.SRC / CTAttached.SNK are port detaches: Transitions to `CTUnattached.SNK` are not power role swaps, but the CTVPD remains attached to the port until `CTUnattached.SNK` -\u003e `Unattached.SNK`.",
      "parentUuid": "e924cf40_113fca76",
      "revId": "d17e7f95f390ef91a87088544044bb389d668b39",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "235b20ee_e7e6d778",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 2177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T23:39:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. Would it work to have something like `tc_state_is_attached(get_last_state_tc())`? That would obviate the flag. Or can you get to a state where you need to detach without coming directly from a restart or from one of the attached states where you set the flag here?",
      "parentUuid": "23863890_e412c60a",
      "revId": "d17e7f95f390ef91a87088544044bb389d668b39",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a1188b2_fc2c6c8d",
